-- check/good: return-type dispatch (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md`
-- §4). `a` is a type, not a value, so `a.decode s` is a dispatch on the type
-- the caller chooses; the `where` clause is what makes it legal (§4.1) and
-- what gives the declaration its one evidence parameter (§7.2). The
-- program is correct, and the interface shows the constraint it carries.
--
pub decode : String -> Result String a
    where a.decode : String -> Result String a
decode s = a.decode s
